  "notes": "The sung counterweight to the rest of this lane, and the three parameters that make it are harmony, register and looseness. Harmony: ninth 0.4 with triad 0.1 is the most extended chord vocabulary in this batch by a distance, because the research names m9, maj7 and add9 as the palette. Register: `bassline.rhythm` is `offbeat_8ths` over E1–C3 at `followRootsProb` 0.6 — the research says rounded synth or electric bass playing syncopated 8ths under the changes, not an 808 riff, so the sub is reinforcement and the part is a real bass line. Looseness: `quantizeStrength` 0.66 with 6–9 ms of jitter across the kit is the research’s “live-feel timing rather than gridded”, and it is the loosest model in this batch. The vocal melody being the primary content is authored as `intervals.step` 0.74 with `leap` 0.06 and `arch` 0.45 — small intervals with one leap per phrase — and the stacked background harmony is `countermelody.densityRatio` 0.55 with octave_echo weighted equal to arp. ⚠ `medium`: the research measures only two tempo/key points (124 E, 144 F♯m), so the 118–146 band is an interpolation between them and the harmonic and kit claims are marked [LOW-CONF] where not directly sourced. ⚠ The keys B and C♯m are INFERRED sharp-side neighbours of the two documented centres; the research names only F♯ minor and E major. ⚠ The 8-bar sung chorus is spelled `hook` because that is the section name every generator in this project reads. ⚠ **`lockTo808` raised from 0.35 to 0.61.** The 808 takes each kick with this probability, and at 0.35 over this model's 8-kick floor a seed could produce no 808 at all — which `bass808.rs` refuses, because a declared 808 that sometimes vanishes is a part a producer cannot rely on. It is still well under a lock: a good share of kicks carry no sub. ⚠ The bass ceiling came down from 48 to 45 so it stays under a chord part that starts at 46 — `coherence.rs` requires the highest bass note to sit at or below the lowest chord note, and this model overlapped by 3.",
